!
! One device's energy (homestead_rules.h HR4), in Trebago: the exact sum
! of the readings in watt-hours whose device is want, added from the first.
! A reading counts when both 1 + device - want and 1 + want - device are
! at least 1, that is when its device is want. A partial sum past 64 bits
! is refused, never wrapped; energy.kron adds from the last, so a sum that
! passes 64 bits one way only is held.
trebago device_energy
  in  device(n), want, wh(n)
  out energy
  energy = sum(i, max(0, min(1, 1 + device(i) - want)) * max(0, min(1, 1 + want - device(i))) * wh(i))
end
